Evicts from leveldb's LRU cache when an entry is released and its shard is over capacity, as
Insert does (#2316). Insert evicts only entries no one holds, and the block it inserts is held
until its read is done, so a block larger than the shard stayed until the next Insert into that
shard. Chromium's shared block cache is 8 MiB in 16 shards of 512 KiB, and uBlock Origin's
chrome.storage.local reads multi-MB blocks at launch, so up to 16 of them sat in the browser
process: 21-39 MiB, against Chrome's 0, on the perf run's hosted runners. leveldb is
google/leveldb at the commit Chromium's DEPS pins, under its BSD licence.

--- a/third_party/leveldatabase/src/util/cache.cc
+++ b/third_party/leveldatabase/src/util/cache.cc
@@ -234,6 +234,17 @@
     // No longer in use; move to lru_ list.
     LRU_Remove(e);
     LRU_Append(&lru_, e);
+    // browser_core: an entry larger than the shard's capacity outlives its own
+    // Insert, as it's in use then, so it's evicted once released rather than at
+    // the shard's next Insert, which may never come (#2316).
+    while (usage_ > capacity_ && lru_.next != &lru_) {
+      LRUHandle* old = lru_.next;
+      assert(old->refs == 1);
+      bool erased = FinishErase(table_.Remove(old->key(), old->hash));
+      if (!erased) {  // to avoid unused variable when compiled NDEBUG
+        assert(erased);
+      }
+    }
   }
 }
 
